// Title: Lsass Full Dump Request Via DumpType Registry Settings
// Sigma ID: 33efc23c-6ea2-4503-8cfe-bdf82ce8f719
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @pbssubhash
// Date: 2022-12-08 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.001
// Description: Detects the setting of the "DumpType" registry value to "2" which stands for a "Full Dump".
//   Technique such as LSASS Shtinkering requires this value to be "2" in order to dump LSASS.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate application that needs to do a full dump of their process
// References:
//   - https://github.com/deepinstinct/Lsass-Shtinkering
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/wer/collecting-user-mode-dumps
//   - https://media.defcon.org/DEF%20CON%2030/DEF%20CON%2030%20presentations/Asaf%20Gilboa%20-%20LSASS%20Shtinkering%20Abusing%20Windows%20Error%20Reporting%20to%20Dump%20LSASS.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_lsass_usermode_dumping.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Error Reporting\\LocalDumps\\DumpType" or RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Error Reporting\\LocalDumps\\lsass.exe\\DumpType") and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000002)"
